# Vendored third-party trees. Every nested clone here carries its own .git and
# is ignored wholesale (Sesame CSM, CityWalker, fish-speech, llama.cpp, ...).
#
# THE ONE CARVE-OUT (card GATE-0, scrum/20260822/task_20): both product scenes
# `<include>` the Unitree Go2 MJCF at
# `third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/go2.xml`, so a blanket ignore
# made a fresh clone unable to compile `city_block.xml` at all — `ci_gate.py
# --tier commit` died ~1 s in with an unhandled ValueError and never emitted a
# summary. The 20-file manifest-pinned subset below (LICENSE, PROVENANCE.json,
# two MJCF files, 16 OBJ meshes; 27.1 MiB) is therefore TRACKED, at its
# upstream path so the scenes' include lines and the frozen scene digests do
# not move. `tests/test_unitree_asset_pack.py` + the `unitree-assets` gate
# stage enforce exact closure: an unmanifested file here is a hard red.
# Nothing else under third_party/ — including the nested .git directories and
# the 296 MB developer checkout this subset came from — is exposed.
third_party/*
!third_party/unitree_mujoco/
third_party/unitree_mujoco/*
!third_party/unitree_mujoco/LICENSE
!third_party/unitree_mujoco/PROVENANCE.json
!third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/
third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/*
!third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/
third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/*
!third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/go2.xml
!third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/scene.xml
!third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/assets/
third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/assets/*
!third_party/unitree_mujoco/unitree_robots/go2/assets/*.obj
/usr/

.tmp_ci/
.tmp/
